Pusula model weights are LoRA adapters and a code readout trained on top of vllm-sr/d3 (Pusula)
and a fine-tuned TabiBERT cross-encoder (Pusula Nano).

Data provenance. Pusula models were trained primarily on synthetic Turkish data generated for this
project. A limited set of real customer messages, licensed from a commercial partner, was also
included in the training data. These messages were anonymized prior to use and are not redistributed
in any form.

Classifications used to diversify the synthetic data (version 2.0). The sectors and occupations of the
synthetic messages were sampled from the following classifications. They are not redistributed.
- NACE Rev. 2.1, the statistical classification of economic activities in the European Community.
  Source: Eurostat. © European Union. Reused under Commission Decision 2011/833/EU.
- ESCO (European Skills, Competences, Qualifications and Occupations), occupations pillar.
